BT 1 0 0 1 0 42.7 Tm /F1 9.3 Tf 13 TL 1.891383 Tw (An online shopping cart is one of the most common examples of data structures working together in a real) Tj T* 0 Tw .893163 Tw (application. Every shop needs a fast catalogue lookup, a cart that grows as the customer adds items, a way to) Tj T* 0 Tw .806771 Tw (undo the most recent addition, and a way to present the cart in a useful order. Each of these needs matches a) Tj T* 0 Tw (classic data structure: hashing, linked list, stack and sorting.) Tj T* ET
